  "scope": "The whole theorem of Federer 3.2.23, p. 260: genuinely m-rectifiable Borel W and finite (H^mu,mu)-rectifiable Borel Z have a finite (H^(m+mu),m+mu)-rectifiable Cartesian product. Under the usual Euclidean block identification its entire restricted Hausdorff measure equals the product of the factor restrictions on every test subset, not only rectangles. All natural dimensions are retained, including multipoint zero-dimensional factors, with no dimension inequality or bound by ambient dimension.",
